Y\tab\tab\tab    The \ul Y\ulnone ank command reads some portion of the input file into the\par
                     edit buffer.  Since <FF> checking has been inhibited, only the\par
                     currently available buffer size determines the exact quantity\par
                     read in at any point.  TECO implementations vary as to exact\par
                     edit buffer size; a number of additional locations are\par
                     generally reserved in case the edit buffer grows larger.\par
\par
                     Note: Typical usage of the STRIP.TEC program will generally\par
                     maintain the overall file size; certain specific operations\par
                     might tend to raise or lower the overall size (slightly)\par
                     depending on specific file contents.  Most character\par
                     processing consists of merely clearing the high-order (mark\par
                     parity) bit.  As such, the overall character count tends to \par
                     remain (relatively) constant.\par
\par
