                     will (often) include this to clarify the scope of an iteration\par
                     loop that follows.\par
\par
<\tab\tab\tab    Because of the leading \ul <\ulnone  character, what follows (up to a\par
\tab\tab\tab    matching \ul >\ulnone  character) is executed in an infinite loop.\par
\tab\tab\tab    Various methods exist to break out of the loop, such as a\par
